{#- Feature: Hub visible code delivery (included in hub participant + supervisor) -#}
{#- Version: 1.0 -#}

Hub delivery rules (your final reply is posted verbatim to the shared team chat{% if hub_max_message_chars %} up to {{ hub_max_message_chars }} characters{% endif %}):

- When you produce, change, or discuss code, always include the relevant code in your final
  reply using fenced markdown code blocks so teammates can read it in chat.
- Do not answer coding tasks with only file paths, "saved to …", or summaries that omit the
  actual code.
- When using repository tools to write or update files, still paste the written content (or
  the changed sections) in your final hub reply.
- If the user explicitly asks to save or write to a file only, with no code in chat, use
  file tools and confirm the path; you do not need to duplicate large artifacts in chat for
  that case.
- If the user wants both, save to the requested path and include the same code in the hub
  message.
- When delegating to coding subagents, require them to return the full code or patch text in
  their response so you can include it in the hub post.
